Implemented `decode_prefix`, `decode_exact`, `serialize`, and `identify` in
Zig 0.16.0, using only the standard library. No external specifications,
Bitcoin libraries, reference programs, evaluator access, or network access
were used.

The separate repair phase used only the existing materials and the supplied
`feedback.json`. All six feedback responses now match completely. The repair
changes amounts to signed 64-bit values throughout parsing, serialization,
decoding, and identification, and checks impossible declared collection
lengths before applying `max_items`.

